&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Come join the organization that is redefining security for the AI era. As one of the&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wiz.io/blog/100m-arr-in-18-months-wiz-becomes-the-fastest-growing-software-company-ever&quot;&gt; fastest-growing startups ever,&lt;/a&gt; we enable teams to secure cloud and AI applications by connecting code, cloud, and runtime into a single shared context. Trusted by security teams all over the world, we have a proven&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.g2.com/products/wiz-wiz/reviews&quot;&gt; track record of success&lt;/a&gt; and a culture that values world-class talent. Not to mention, we&#39;re now&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/identity-security/google-completes-acquisition-of-wiz&quot;&gt; powered by Google&lt;/a&gt;, meaning we offer our customers an AI-powered platform that harnesses Google’s Threat Intelligence and Security Operations to better detect, prevent, and respond to threats across all environments, allowing for further innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Wizards from all over the globe work together to protect the infrastructure of our customers, including over 65% of the Fortune 100, who trust us to scan and secure over 230 billion files daily. We’re honored to be a leading player in a massive and growing market, and we continue to look for exceptional Wizards who are eager to make a significant impact on our team. At Wiz, you’ll have the freedom to think creatively, dream big, and use your full range of skills to contribute to our momentous growth. Come join our team and help us create secure cloud environments that allow even the best companies to move faster, all while having some fun!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Security Engineering Manager for Product &amp;amp; Production Infrastructure, you will lead and grow a team of talented Security Engineers responsible for protecting cloud-native environments, CI/CD pipelines, and core production infrastructure. In this role, you will act as a technical leader and people manager—providing strategic direction, mentorship, and operational excellence while staying close to modern cloud and container technologies across AWS, Azure, and GCP. You will build deep partnerships with Software Development, DevOps, and Product Management teams to embed secure-by-design principles into developer workflows, drive proactive vulnerability management, and champion our internal dogfooding program to assess, monitor, and influence product roadmaps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Talent Development: Recruit, retain, develop, and coach a high-performing, globally distributed team of Security Engineers; establish performance goals, conduct 1:1s, and support career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Strategy &amp;amp; Architecture: Lead threat modeling and technical security reviews across product architectures and multi-cloud infrastructure to identify attack surfaces and design scalable mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security Automation &amp;amp; &quot;Shift-Left&quot;: Drive the creation of automation, policy-as-code, and developer-friendly security tooling to integrate continuous, end-to-end security checks into CI/CD workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Container Hardening: Define, implement, and govern secure baselines for multi-cloud resources and managed Kubernetes infrastructure (EKS, GKE, AKS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vulnerability &amp;amp; Supply Chain Management: Oversee end-to-end vulnerability management and remediation programs, establishing preventative controls across software supply chains from development to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detection &amp;amp; Incident Response: Partner with detection and response functions to scale alert triage, investigation capabilities, and automated incident remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
